# P114 on Windows, WinUI and GtkBackend: Alt+Left with the caret in a text field still goes Back. A Windows text field moves by word with Ctrl+Left and has no Alt+Left binding; GtkBackend reads Alt+Left in the bubble phase after GtkText, WinUI from its WH_GETMESSAGE hook, and both pop, as Explorer and browsers do. (On macOS Option+Left is the field's word move instead; see mac/P114-textfield-alt-left.actions.)
# Pass: replayed; the log shows depths 1 2 3, note: "ab cdx" (the field had the keys), then depth 2 -- and the note never changes after that.
# P114(Windows,WinUI 與 GtkBackend):插入點在文字框內時 Alt+Left 仍然返回。Windows 文字框用 Ctrl+Left 逐字移動，沒有綁定 Alt+Left;GtkBackend 在 GtkText 之後的 bubble phase 讀 Alt+Left,WinUI 由 WH_GETMESSAGE hook 讀，兩者都彈出，與檔案總管及瀏覽器相同(macOS 上則是文字框的逐字移動，見 mac 版)。通過條件見上方英文。
sleep,,,,,,1500000,let P114 settle,windows
taplabel,,,,,Open Fruits,,push Fruits (depth 1),windows
sleep,,,,,,1200000,,windows
taplabel,,,,,Open Untitled,,push Untitled (depth 2),windows
sleep,,,,,,1200000,,windows
taplabel,,,,,Open Leaf,,push Leaf (depth 3),windows
sleep,,,,,,1200000,,windows
taplabel,,,,,ab cd,,focus Leaf's text field (it holds ab cd),windows
sleep,,,,,,800000,,windows
key,,,,,rightArrow,,caret to the end (extra presses stay at the end),windows
